  "description": "LILXOV crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C50 H50 Er6 N40 O2 Se4,3(C5 H5 N1). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 1 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 1 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 2 O neighbors; Er1A (Er) has 1 O neighbors; Er2A (Er) has 1 O neighbors; Er3A (Er) has 2 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 11 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.501-3.723 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 102.65-111.40°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula (py)10Er6O2(Se2)2+x(N3)10−2x·3(py).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
